00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:04.749
To take a screenshot on a Mac you
quite simply  need to find the folder

00:02:04.779 --> 00:02:08.259
or the document that you wish to take
a screenshot of, make sure that it

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:09.820
is displayed clearly on the screen.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:11.470
And there are two options.

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:13.680
You can take a snapshot
of  everything that's on the

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:15.060
screen at that moment in time.

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:18.210
Or you can specify a specific area.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:22.050
To take a snapshot of exactly what's
on the screen at that time, you

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:27.210
can press the shift key and the
command key and hold those down

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:28.890
and then press the number three.

00:02:30.165 --> 00:02:32.625
You will hear the sound of a
camera clicking, which indicates

00:02:32.625 --> 00:02:34.135
that it has taken  the screenshot.

00:02:34.675 --> 00:02:37.345
You can then go to the Word document.

00:02:37.795 --> 00:02:40.585
In this example, I'm just using a
blank one, but when you're providing

00:02:40.585 --> 00:02:44.005
screenshots, it will primarily
be in your assessment booklet.

00:02:44.545 --> 00:02:48.025
So what I need to do then is hold
down the control key and press V.

00:02:48.625 --> 00:02:50.875
And that will provide the screenshot.

00:02:51.025 --> 00:02:54.685
So it's basically took a picture of
what was on the screen, and that as

00:02:54.685 --> 00:02:57.265
now being entered into the document.

